  "method": "Volumes are the vented-or-flared column on the Railroad Commission Form PR tapes posted September 26, 2026. Oil rows are olf102 and gas rows are gsf102. Each lease uses its latest month on that tape. MMcfd is that month's Mcf divided by the number of days in the month, then by 1,000. The circle is the centroid of RRC surface wells on that lease. The lease number is the gas or oil id directly before the field name, and the field name is the 32 characters before the completion date on the September 23, 2026 API extract. Both the lease name and the field name have to match the Form PR row. Lease numbers are matched only in Railroad Commission districts 05, 7B, and 09. The county set is the 25 Texas counties the Commission lists for the Newark, East (Barnett Shale) field. Oklahoma and Louisiana are not included. Pipelines are the EIA centerline compilation from January 2020, clipped to the bounding box of these counties. Transmission lines are the public 230 kV-and-above subset in the project database, clipped the same way. Points of interconnection are substations and taps of 69 kV and above that fall inside these counties. Counties drawn: Archer, Bosque, Clay, Comanche, Cooke, Coryell, Dallas, Denton, Eastland, Ellis, Erath, Hamilton, Hill, Hood, Jack, Johnson, Montague, Palo Pinto, Parker, Shackelford, Somervell, Stephens, Tarrant, Wise, Young.",
